From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:52:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: fs/resctrl: Continue IOMMU group migration
 after errors

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167008

rdt_move_group_iommus() stops walking IOMMU groups after the first migration
error. Its callers discard the return value and continue tearing down the
resctrl group, so later IOMMU groups can retain stale CLOSID and RMID values.

Continue walking after per-group failures while preserving the first error as
the return value. Advancing kset_get_next_obj() releases the iterator reference
for the previous object, so remove the explicit error-path kobject_put()
together with the break.

Fixes: 0f5b95aa592b ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: fs/resctrl: Migrate IOMMU groups when removing resource groups")
Signed-off-by: Lee Trager <ltrager@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 40a4166779fef1789c766f7df812e5ef52b7eb30 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00615
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@d3ebad16a9fc768423f4ccf3083df9ae214cea5d
---
 fs/resctrl/rdtgroup.c | 10 ++++------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/resctrl/rdtgroup.c b/fs/resctrl/rdtgroup.c
index c20790ee5e3b..76ae5c87afc3 100644
--- a/fs/resctrl/rdtgroup.c
+++ b/fs/resctrl/rdtgroup.c
@@ -3252,7 +3252,7 @@ static int rdt_move_group_iommus(struct rdtgroup *from, struct rdtgroup *to)
 {
 	struct kset *iommu_groups;
 	struct iommu_group *group;
-	int err = 0, iommu_group_id;
+	int err, ret = 0, iommu_group_id;
 	struct kobject *group_kobj = NULL;
 
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_RESCTRL_IOMMU))
@@ -3275,17 +3275,15 @@ static int rdt_move_group_iommus(struct rdtgroup *from, struct rdtgroup *to)
 			err = kstrtoint(group_kobj->name, 0, &iommu_group_id);
 			if (!err)
 				err = rdtgroup_move_iommu(iommu_group_id, to);
+			if (err && !ret)
+				ret = err;
 		}
 
 		iommu_group_put(group);
-		if (err) {
-			kobject_put(group_kobj);
-			break;
-		}
 	}
 
 	kset_put(iommu_groups);
-	return err;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static void free_all_child_rdtgrp(struct rdtgroup *rdtgrp)
